  "write_verbs_note": "THE verb table. Each row is a typed command from crates/vault/src/commands/* (or one of GRAMMAR.md 2.7's two verb CLASSES, reschedule/delete), with `sense` stating the ACT the command performs and `surfaces` the English verbs that name that act. The surfaces were written from the sense — the ordinary ways a person says `declare a task finished`, `put a row back after binning it`, `record money spent` — and NOT read off any corpus sentence; the corpora were consulted only to learn WHICH senses were unreachable. `needs` is an any-of guard for a surface too generic to stand alone (`add` is a task, a note, an expense, an album entry or a group member until a second word says which). `bars` rules a row out. `question_ok` lets a row fire behind an interrogative opener, which only a disclosure request legitimately is.",

